package pages

import "strconv"

// bonusEntry is one row of a bonus grid: the suffix that makes the form field
// name, the three-letter abbreviation printed under the name, and the name.
type bonusEntry struct {
	Key   string
	Abbr  string
	Label string
}

// bonusRow is the row shared by the saving throws and skills grids. The two
// tables were separate components with byte-identical row markup and two copies
// of the same stylesheet, which is exactly the duplication the move to
// server-rendered markup is meant to remove -- so the row is defined once here
// and the tables supply only their entries and their own grid.
//
// The stack is a real <label for> plus a plain <span>, not the <span class="label">
// the lit-html components used. That span was the last thing in the app holding
// DaisyUI's .label class name, and retiring it is what emptied the exclusions in
// css/app.css. The <label> also buys an accessible name and a click target that
// the aria-label it replaces did not.
//
// The abbreviation is text-base-content/75, the muted standard already used on
// the character cards. On the sheet's bg-base-200/85 panel that measures 4.68
// caramellatte / 4.57 coffee against 4.5 for AA. Worth knowing it is close: over
// one of the desk's grid rules the coffee figure falls to 4.49, which is where
// the 4.36 recorded against D2 in phase 2 came from. Full base-content would be
// 7.14 but flattens the hierarchy the old sheet had between name and ability.
//
// No min/max and no .validator, both carried over from the components this
// replaces. A bonus is signed, so there is no floor to declare; with no
// constraint to violate the only rule left is step="1", whose one failure mode
// is a typed decimal. Wiring .validator for that would buy a red border with
// nowhere to put a hint, and would paint a :user-valid green border on every
// filled field across a tight grid for the normal case. The text and number
// fields carry it because they have required/min/max and room for a line of text.
templ bonusRow(field string, label string, abbr string, value int) {
	<div class="flex items-center justify-between gap-2 rounded-field border-2 border-base-300 p-2">
		<span class="flex min-w-0 flex-col gap-0.5">
			<label class="text-sm font-medium" for={ field }>{ label }</label>
			<span class="text-xs font-semibold tracking-wider text-base-content/75">{ abbr }</span>
		</span>
		<input
			id={ field }
			name={ field }
			type="number"
			inputmode="numeric"
			step="1"
			class="input input-sm w-14 text-right"
			value={ strconv.Itoa(value) }
		/>
	</div>
}
